.ie n \{\
 .  ds ... \(bu
 .\}
.el \{\
 .  ds ... \(em
.\}
.TH "TARSNAP.CONF" "5" "2026-10-12" "Tarsnap Backup" "User Manuals"
.ad l
.SH NAME
tarsnap.conf \- tarsnap configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtarsnap\fR
.RS
.PP
Reads configuration from
.I @sysconfdir@/tarsnap.conf
and
.IR ~/.tarsnaprc .
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tarsnap
configuration file is a simple text file containing one option per
line.
A line beginning with the character
.Ql #
is treated as a comment.
Options are specified as name\-value pairs, separated by a single space
character.
For options that do not accept a value (flags), only the name is
specified.
The following options may be specified:
.TP
\fBgzip\-compression\fP \fIX\fP
.TP
\fBmaxbw\fP
.TP
\fBmaxbw-rate-down\fP
.TP
\fBmaxbw-rate-up\fP
.TP
\fBnoatime\fP
.TP
\fBnodump\fP
.TP
\fBnormalmem\fP
.TP
\fBno-aggressive-networking\fP
.TP
\fBno-backup-metadata\fP
.TP
\fBno-compression-sample\fP
.TP
\fBno-cpupri\fP
.TP
\fBno\-debug\fP
.TP
\fBno-force-tar\fP
.TP
\fBno\-list\-all\-keyfiles\fP
.TP
\fBno-print-stats\fP
.TP
\fBno\-quiet\fP
.TP
\fBno-retry-forever\fP
.TP
\fBno-snaptime\fP
.TP
\fBno-store-atime\fP
.TP
\fBno\-totals\fP
.TP
\fBpassphrase\fP \fImethod:arg\fP
.TP
\fBprint-stats\fP
.TP
\fBprogress-bytes\fP \fIX\fP
.TP
\fBquiet\fP
.TP
\fBretry-forever\fP
.TP
\fBsnaptime\fP \fIfile\fP
.SH FILES
.ad l
.RS 5
.TP
.I @sysconfdir@/tarsnap.conf
System\-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.tarsnaprc
User\-specific configuration file.
.RE
.SH NOTES
Note that the
.B no-*
options are only useful in the user-specific
.I ~/.tarsnaprc
configuration file, at which point they act to override options set in the
global
.I @sysconfdir@/tarsnap.conf
configuration file.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR tarsnap (1)
.SH AUTHOR
.nf
Ian Goldberg <ian@cse.uwaterloo.ca>
.na
